Preserve real main/callback C continuations for observed audio service inputs.

The actual original replay trace contains main-thread controls inside a timer
callback lifetime. Run the port callback on its own cooperative stack and suspend
it at an API boundary while the main engine supplies intervening calls. API
arguments, statuses, cursors and gains remain assertions of engine calculations.
Native uses ucontext with ASan stack-switch annotations; browser uses Emscripten
fibers/Asyncify. Synchronous Node explicitly rejects interleaved inputs. Inputs
without interleaving retain the inline path. This enables diagnosis; it does not
establish full original replay-engine or physical timing equivalence.

